{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-161508",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is the vector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
